course: dictionary
lesson: 282
title: Names and titles with capital letters
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word with a capital letter can be a name, and some names are also words with their own meanings. «Amir guesses the globe has like 300 countries.» Here Amir is a boy's name, so it starts with a capital letter.
explain: Amir can also be a word for a ruler, prince or commander in some Muslim countries, especially in the Middle East. It is sometimes spelled emir. In a history or geography lesson, amir is in the title of rulers such as the amir of Qatar or Kuwait.
explain: To tell which meaning is right, read the clues around the word. Is it a person's name, or a title for a ruler? Then swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Amir is a noun. It can be a boy's name, or a word for a ruler or commander.
fact: As a name, Amir is written with a capital letter.
fact: An amir (also spelled emir) is a ruler, prince or commander in some Muslim countries, especially in the Middle East.
fact: In history and geography lessons, amir appears in the titles of rulers of countries such as Qatar and Kuwait.
fact: Amir is a common first name for boys in many countries.
exercise: «Amir guesses the globe has like 300 countries.» In this sentence, what is Amir? | A kind of globe | A prince in a history book | A ruler of a country | *A boy's name
exercise: In a history lesson about Kuwait, amir is a title. What does it mean there? | A type of boat | *A ruler or prince of a country | A school subject | A boy who is always late
exercise: Which other spelling can amir have? | amor | amire | admire | *emir
test: In «Amir guesses the globe has like 300 countries», why does Amir start with a capital letter? | Because it comes after a full stop | Because it is a country | *Because it is a name | Because it starts a new page
test: Which word is another spelling of amir? | amber | amp | *emir | admire
exam: Which is the best meaning of amir as a title? | *A ruler, prince or commander in some Muslim countries | A boy who is always late | A type of fish | A large, flat stone
